Third-party source and reference inventory
==========================================

This package remains licensed under GPL-3. The following incorporated portions
are also subject to the preserved upstream MIT notice below.

Adapted from dplyr 1.2.1:
  Revision: 95740975c465c29cdb2abdfa13effddb948444dc
  Source: https://github.com/tidyverse/dplyr/tree/95740975c465c29cdb2abdfa13effddb948444dc
  R/select.R: select.data.frame(), ensure_group_vars()
  R/rename.R: rename.data.frame()
  R/relocate.R: relocate.data.frame(), eval_relocate()
  R/grouped-df.R: [.grouped_df and names<-.grouped_df policies
  R/rowwise.R: [.rowwise_df and names<-.rowwise_df policies
  Destinations: R/dibble-result.R and the select, rename, and relocate methods
    in R/mutate-data.R.
  Changes: package-owned column-list assembly and result finalization replace
    whole-table dplyr dispatch. Existing dibble typing, metadata, isolation and
    capacity rules apply. Selector helpers use qualified public tidyselect,
    rlang and base R functions. Group retention and renaming are explicit.
  Tests: public selector cases adapted into tests/testthat/test-dibble-columns.R
    from tests/testthat/test-select.R, test-rename.R and test-relocate.R,
    with Stata-typed fixtures and additional dibble ownership assertions.
  The inspected files contain no separate file-level copyright or license.

Studied as references only, with no dtplyr implementation incorporated:
  dtplyr 1.3.3, revision 2cc627511c34ed461093ae4c5dc94faccffeb93c
  https://github.com/tidyverse/dtplyr/tree/2cc627511c34ed461093ae4c5dc94faccffeb93c
  R/step-subset-select.R, R/step-call.R, R/step-subset.R, and their tests.
  Selection plans and copy flags informed the design review. They do not
  establish the ownership or symmetric isolation required by dibbles. The
  inspected files contain no separate file-level notices. dtplyr's MIT license
  is reproduced for reference; this is not a claim that its code was copied.

Public tidyselect, rlang, vctrs, tibble and dplyr APIs remain dependencies.
Calling those APIs does not incorporate their implementations. No vctrs or
data.table source was copied or adapted for this stage.

